{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"2576dc18bef42bdd5fbb46cf7b94f28bab7eedc2afb9c275ca66ae15f00d3b24","packTokens":13618,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":255,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":407,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":792,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":1549,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":341,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":10159,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-01T12:08:25.802Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261001-invoice-reminders-a-small-06fa\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"payments\",\n  \"public-api\",\n  \"auth\",\n  \"pii\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"Mark invoices overdue after 7 days past due date and show on overdue list\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"Staff can send email reminders to customers with invoice details\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"System records reminder history with sender and timestamp\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"Handle and display email delivery failures\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Filter overdue list by customer and days overdue\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-6\",\n   \"text\": \"Build overdue list screen with send reminder buttons\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-7\",\n   \"text\": \"Build invoice detail screen with reminder history\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can view the overdue list and send reminders, and where do staff accounts come from?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Is an invoice exactly 7 days past its due date overdue, or does it only become overdue from day 8?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Overdue from day 7 (today >= due date + 7)\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Does reminder history record only successful sends, or every attempt including failures?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt, each with a delivery status (sent / failed + reason)\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope, so how does an invoice leave the overdue list (for example, once it is paid)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A paid/closed status in the existing invoice data removes it automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Can staff send another reminder for an invoice that was already reminded, and how do we stop accidental double clicks?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Repeat reminders allowed at any time; only accidental double submits are blocked\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should 'overdue' be worked out each time from the due date and paid status, or saved as a status on the invoice record?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Worked out each time; nothing is written to invoices\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where does the customer's email address come from, and what happens if there isn't one or there are several?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Single email field on the existing customer record; block sending if missing\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What counts as a 'delivery failure' that gets recorded with a reason?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Send-time errors plus later bounces reported back by the provider\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-7\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Where do invoices and customers come from? The request mentions the client's existing .NET 8 API, but no repository was found. → assumed: They already exist in the client's API and Postgres database; we read them from there\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Is the overdue status saved by a scheduled job, or worked out from the due date each time it is needed? → assumed: Worked out from due date and today's date each time it is queried\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Is the 7-day overdue threshold fixed in code or a configuration setting? → assumed: Configuration setting, default 7\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How is 'days overdue' counted for display and filtering? → assumed: Days since the due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What kind of input is the days-overdue filter? → assumed: Fixed buckets (7–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service sends reminders, and what counts as a delivery failure? → assumed: Transactional provider (e.g. SendGrid/Postmark) with send errors plus bounces reported later by webhook\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which address does a reminder go to, and what if the customer has none or several? → assumed: One billing email on the customer record; sending is blocked with an error if it is missing\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Who supplies the reminder email wording and the from address? → assumed: Client provides wording; template stored in config\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which timezone is used to decide what day it is for the overdue calculation? → assumed: The business's local timezone (configured)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the 7-day threshold be fixed in the code or a setting? → assumed: App setting (config file/env)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which timezone defines 'today' when checking due date + 7 days? → assumed: The business's local timezone (fixed setting)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should emails be sent? → assumed: The client's existing email service/SMTP relay\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How should accidental double submits be blocked (from Q-5)? → assumed: Client disable plus a server-side check that rejects a second send for the same invoice within a short window (e.g. 60s)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the 'days overdue' filter work, and what is it counted from? → assumed: Preset ranges past due date (7–14, 15–30, 30+)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Who decides the wording, sender address and language of the reminder email? → assumed: A fixed template we draft, approved by the client\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-4\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-16\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Can reminders only be sent from the overdue list, or also from the invoice detail screen (for example, to retry after a failure)? → assumed: Both overdue list and invoice detail\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-01T12:08:25.829Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261001-invoice-reminders-a-small-06fa\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-1 (high risk): invoices, customers, the paid/closed status and the customer email field already exist in the client's .NET 8 API and Postgres database and are read from there. No repository was available, so every requirement is ADDED and all endpoint paths and field names (e.g. GET /api/overdue-invoices or /api/invoices/overdue, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders, POST /api/email-events or /api/email-provider/events) are placeholders to be mapped to the real API.\",\n  \"Days-overdue buckets: ASM-5 (7–30/31–60/61–90/90+) is used over ASM-14 (7–14/15–30/30+), with the top bucket starting at 91 so buckets don't overlap. The client must confirm.\",\n  \"Email channel: ASM-6 (transactional provider with signed bounce webhooks) is used over ASM-12 (existing SMTP relay), because Q-8 needs bounces reported back and a plain SMTP relay can't reliably do that. The client must confirm.\",\n  \"Email template: the wording and from address come from a configured template; ASM-8 (client provides wording) and ASM-15 (we draft, client approves) are combined. The body must contain invoice number, amount and due date.\",\n  \"The overdue threshold is an app setting with default 7 (ASM-3/ASM-10). Today's date comes from a configured business timezone (ASM-9/ASM-11). Days overdue counts whole calendar days from the due date (ASM-4), so an invoice first appears on the list with days overdue = 7.\",\n  \"The double-submit window is 60 seconds, checked per invoice on the server (ASM-13), counting from the previous accepted request that reached the provider, whatever the provider outcome. Duplicates rejected this way are not recorded in reminder history.\",\n  \"Requests blocked before any provider call (missing email, not overdue, duplicate, unauthenticated) are not delivery attempts and create no reminder history entry; Q-3's 'every attempt' is read as every attempt that reaches the provider.\",\n  \"The provider gives each send a message id that is stored on the reminder history entry and used to match bounce events; the webhook is authenticated by the provider's signature against a configured secret, not by staff authentication.\",\n  \"The sender recorded in history is the identity of the authenticated user from the existing API authentication.\",\n  \"Error status codes (400, 401, 404, 409, 422, 502) are proposals; the client API's own error conventions take priority if they differ.\",\n  \"Reminder history is shown newest first. Reminders can be sent from both the overdue list and the invoice detail screen (ASM-16).\"\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 10,000 invoices and 1,000 customers in the database, with or without filters\",\n   \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 500 customers\",\n   \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"Endpoint returns within 10 s in 100% of calls; provider call timeout ≤ 8 s\",\n   \"text\": \"The send-reminder endpoint gives the staff user a result within a fixed time, including when the provider is slow (d1 reading).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"Provider call timeout 10 s; endpoint returns within 12 s in 100% of requests\",\n   \"text\": \"The send-reminder endpoint does not hang on a slow email provider (d2 reading).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 5 s; provider call timeout 10 s, after which the attempt is recorded as failed\",\n   \"text\": \"Send-reminder endpoint response time including the provider call (d3 reading).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n   \"metric\": \"≥ 99% of valid bounce webhook events reflected in the reminder history status within 60 s of receipt\",\n   \"text\": \"Bounce reports from the provider show up in reminder history soon after they arrive.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 occurrences of customer email addresses in application log output during a full run of the acceptance test suite\",\n   \"text\": \"Customer email addresses (PII) are not written to application logs.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 reminder history rows deleted or overwritten by the application, other than the status/reason update from a bounce; rows kept for at least 7 years\",\n   \"text\": \"Every reminder attempt is kept for audit.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 duplicate provider send calls when 10 concurrent requests for the same invoice arrive within 1 s\",\n   \"text\": \"No duplicate emails come from double submits.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Payments and recording payments or marking invoices paid (invoices leave the list only through the paid/closed status already in the invoice data)\",\n  \"Customer logins or any customer-facing screens\",\n  \"SMS reminders\",\n  \"Automatic or scheduled reminders that no staff user triggers\",\n  \"Saving or writing an overdue flag/status on invoice records\",\n  \"More than one email address per customer, or choosing a recipient\",\n  \"Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user'\",\n  \"Editing the email template from the UI (template is stored in config)\",\n  \"Creating or editing invoices and customer records, including customer email addresses\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 200 and contains INV-1\",\n     \"when\": \"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due)\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response does not contain INV-2\",\n     \"when\": \"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response contains INV-3\",\n     \"when\": \"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10 and today is 2026-10-15\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"an open invoice due 2026-10-05 is included and an open invoice due 2026-10-06 is not\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that is not paid or closed and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"invoice C is 30 days past its due date with status paid and invoice D is 30 days past its due date with status closed\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"neither C nor D is in the response\",\n     \"when\": \"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"INV-6 is no longer in the response, with no other action needed\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested again\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice has a paid or closed status in the existing invoice data, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list whatever its due date.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list endpoint and the invoice detail endpoint for an overdue invoice are called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders API shall work out overdue status when it is queried and shall not write any overdue flag or status to invoice records.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"ASM-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"today is 2026-10-15 in the business timezone and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, is due 2026-10-01\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the INV-100 entry has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 14\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"today is 2026-09-08 and open invoice INV-1 is due 2026-09-01 with threshold 7\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the INV-1 entry has days overdue 7\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"3 overdue invoices and 2 invoices that are not overdue\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response contains exactly the 3 overdue invoices\",\n     \"when\": \"an authenticated staff user calls GET the overdue list endpoint\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return, for each overdue invoice, its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"customer A has 2 overdue invoices and customer B has 3 overdue invoices\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer A\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"customer C has no overdue invoices\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 200 with an empty list\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"7–30 returns 7 and 30; 31–60 returns 31 and 60; 61–90 returns 61 and 90; 90+ returns only 91\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with each bucket in turn\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days and customer B has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"only customer A's 40-day invoice is returned\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"any data\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 400 and names the allowed bucket values\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets (e.g. 5-9)\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or 91 and over (90+), the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue falls inside that bucket, bounds included.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"no authentication credentials\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body, the email provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are each called\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"an expired or invalid staff token and an overdue invoice\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"both responses are 401 and the email provider stub receives no call\",\n     \"when\": \"the overdue list endpoint and the send-reminder endpoint for that invoice are called\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to the overdue list, invoice detail or send-reminder endpoint has no valid staff authentication under the existing API's authentication scheme, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401, return no invoice or customer data, and send no email.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-100 (amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01) belongs to a customer with email accounts@crumb.example, and a stubbed email provider\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 2xx and the provider stub receives exactly one send request addressed to accounts@crumb.example whose body contains 'INV-100', '250.00' and '2026-10-01'\",\n     \"when\": \"the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"the template in configuration is changed to a different subject line\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the provider stub receives the new subject line\",\n     \"when\": \"a reminder is sent\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has an email address, the invoice reminders API shall send one email through the configured transactional email provider to the single email address on the customer record, using the configured template and containing the invoice number, amount and due date.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-16\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-200 belongs to a customer whose email field is empty\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 422 with a message saying the customer has no email address, the provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\",\n     \"when\": \"the send-reminder endpoint for INV-200 is called with a valid staff token\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If the customer record of the invoice has no email address, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the send-reminder request with HTTP 422 and an error saying the customer has no email address, shall not call the email provider, and shall not record a reminder history entry.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"ASM-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"invoice INV-21 has status paid\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 409 saying the invoice is not overdue, and the email provider stub receives no request\",\n     \"when\": \"the send-reminder endpoint for INV-21 is called with a valid staff token\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request is for an invoice that is not currently overdue, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the request with HTTP 409 and an error saying the invoice is not overdue, and shall not call the email provider.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"I-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"staff user 'sam' is authenticated, INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email, and the provider stub accepts the send\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"a reminder history row exists for INV-100 with sender 'sam', timestamp 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z (±5 s), status 'sent' and an empty failure reason\",\n     \"when\": \"sam sends a reminder for INV-100 at 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"two reminders were sent for INV-100 more than 60 seconds apart by 'maria' and then 'tom'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"two separate entries exist with senders 'maria' and 'tom' and their own timestamps\",\n     \"when\": \"the reminder history for INV-100 is read\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a reminder send is attempted with the email provider, the invoice reminders API shall store a reminder history entry holding the invoice, the authenticated staff user who sent it, the UTC timestamp of the attempt, and a delivery status of sent or failed with a failure reason when failed.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"overdue invoice INV-100 and a provider stub that rejects the send with 'invalid recipient'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 502 including 'invalid recipient', a reminder history row for INV-100 has status 'failed' and reason 'invalid recipient', and the overdue list still contains INV-100\",\n     \"when\": \"the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a provider stub that does not respond within the configured send timeout\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the attempt is recorded as 'failed' with a reason that says it timed out and an error response is returned\",\n     \"when\": \"a reminder is sent for INV-100\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If the email provider returns an error or does not respond within the send timeout when a reminder is sent, then the invoice reminders API shall record the attempt as failed with the provider's reason, return an error response containing that reason, and keep the invoice on the overdue list.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a reminder history entry for INV-100 has status 'sent' and provider message id 'msg-1'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 2xx, the entry has status 'failed' and reason 'mailbox does not exist', and INV-100 is still on the overdue list\",\n     \"when\": \"the provider webhook endpoint receives a correctly signed bounce event for 'msg-1' with reason 'mailbox does not exist'\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"no reminder history entry has provider message id 'msg-unknown'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 2xx and no reminder history row changes\",\n     \"when\": \"a correctly signed bounce event for 'msg-unknown' is received\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When the email provider reports a bounce for a reminder previously recorded as sent, the invoice reminders API shall change that reminder history entry's status to failed and store the bounce reason, keeping the invoice on the overdue list.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a reminder history entry recorded as 'sent' with provider message id 'msg-1'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 401 and the entry still has status 'sent'\",\n     \"when\": \"the webhook endpoint receives a bounce event for 'msg-1' whose signature is missing or invalid\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a bounce webhook request fails the email provider's signature verification against the configured secret, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and change no reminder history entry.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the first returns 2xx, the second returns 409, the provider stub receives exactly one send request, and exactly one reminder history row exists for INV-100\",\n     \"when\": \"two send-reminder requests for INV-100 are sent 1 second apart\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a reminder for INV-100 was accepted at 09:00:00\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the request succeeds, a second email is sent and a second history row is recorded\",\n     \"when\": \"another send-reminder request for INV-100 arrives at 09:01:01\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a reminder for INV-100 was accepted 10 seconds ago\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the INV-101 request succeeds and an email is sent\",\n     \"when\": \"a send-reminder request for a different overdue invoice INV-101 is made\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"two send-reminder requests for INV-100 sent at the same moment\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"exactly one reaches the provider and the other returns 409\",\n     \"when\": \"both are processed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request for an invoice arrives within 60 seconds of an earlier accepted send-reminder request for the same invoice, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 409 as a duplicate, shall not call the email provider, and shall not record another reminder history entry.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"INV-100 with amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01, one 'sent' attempt by jo at 2026-10-08T09:00Z and one 'failed' attempt by sam at 2026-10-09T10:00Z with reason 'invalid recipient'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response has invoice number, customer, amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01, the overdue indicator, and history [sam 2026-10-09T10:00Z failed 'invalid recipient', jo 2026-10-08T09:00Z sent with no reason] in that order\",\n     \"when\": \"the invoice detail endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"an invoice with no reminders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response has an empty reminder history\",\n     \"when\": \"its detail is requested\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"invoice id 'does-not-exist'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response is 404\",\n     \"when\": \"the invoice detail endpoint is called for it\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's detail, the invoice reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer, amount, due date, whether it is overdue, and its full reminder history newest first, where each entry shows the sender, timestamp, delivery status and failure reason if there is one.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"a signed-in staff user and 3 overdue invoices for 2 customers\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"the table shows only that customer's invoices in that bucket, with all five columns and a 'Send reminder' button on each row\",\n     \"when\": \"the user opens the overdue list screen, picks one customer in the customer filter and then the 7–30 bucket\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"the email provider stub is set to delay 3 seconds and then fail with 'invalid recipient'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"the button is disabled until the request ends, only one request reaches the API, and the row then shows a failure message containing 'invalid recipient' while the invoice stays in the table\",\n     \"when\": \"the user clicks 'Send reminder' on a row and clicks it again straight away\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"the overdue list screen is open and the provider stub accepts sends\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"a success message is shown for that row once the response arrives\",\n     \"when\": \"the user clicks 'Send reminder' on a row\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The overdue list screen shall show the overdue invoices in a table with invoice number, customer, amount, due date and days overdue, a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, and a 'Send reminder' button on each row that stays disabled while its request is in progress and shows the success or failure result (with reason) when it ends.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-13\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"INV-1 is overdue and has one sent and one failed ('mailbox full') reminder attempt\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"amount and due date are shown, both history entries are listed newest first with sender, time and status, the failed entry shows 'mailbox full', and a 'Send reminder' button is shown\",\n     \"when\": \"a signed-in staff user opens the INV-1 detail screen\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"the invoice detail screen for an overdue invoice\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"a new history entry appears with the user's name, the current time and its delivery status\",\n     \"when\": \"the user clicks 'Send reminder'\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's amount, due date, and reminder history with each attempt's sender, time and delivery status, with each delivery failure and its reason marked out, and a 'Send reminder' button for an overdue invoice.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-16\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"INV-5 is paid\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"no 'Send reminder' button is shown\",\n     \"when\": \"a signed-in staff user opens the INV-5 detail screen\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"While the invoice is not overdue, the invoice detail screen shall not show the 'Send reminder' button.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-16\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"INV-5 is paid\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"a 'Send reminder' button is shown\",\n     \"when\": \"a signed-in staff user opens the INV-5 detail screen\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice detail screen shall show a 'Send reminder' button for any invoice it displays, whether or not the invoice is currently overdue.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-16\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}